A||||11||Philphine||security style torx screws?||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||02-13-2001||11:50 AM||||<BR>the last fiero i got has been modded pretty extensivly. in one spot some torx screws/bolts were used. the thing is they have like a little nipple that sticks up right in the middle so you can't get a torx bit in it. <P>are they maybe some kind of one way screw that can't be taken out once its tightend? even so, some kind of bit would have been needed to tighten it down. i've only tried one hardware store (a big one though) looking for a bit so i'm gonna look some more. i don't want to get impatient and try to drill them out yet. anyone have any experience at all with screws like these? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hartz||02-13-2001||12:01 PM||||Yeah, I've seen those used before.  In fact, I've got one on the center sections of the wheels (OZ Monte Carlos) for my car.  It requires a special "security key" to remove.  If you don't have the key, you may have to drill out the centers to use a regular torx bit.<P>Best of luck,<BR>Hartz<P>'85 SE V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||02-13-2001||12:04 PM||||try <A HREF="http://www.jcwhitney.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jcwhitney.com</A> <P>i think i seen a bit that has a hole in the middle of a torx||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||02-13-2001||12:09 PM||||ok. as long as someones seen it, i should be able to find it. louisville's big enough that some one should have them. if not, i'll look in jc whitney. thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill 88||02-13-2001||12:27 PM|||| They have that type of bit at either the 'Tool King' or the 'Freight Warehouse' tool suppliers (in colorado).  Should be one near you.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||02-13-2001||01:08 PM||||Try Auto-Zone or one of the other chains.  I have seen them in Auto-Zone. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||02-13-2001||01:12 PM||||It is not really a one way screw, those are called "vandal proof screws"  You'll probably see those on outdoor signs and things that people dont want to have ripped off.  Otherwise, the torx screws you refer to are called "security torx".  I have not seen them in the Ace Hardware tool catalog, so dont try there becuase they would even be able to order them.  The last time that I saw them was in a parts express catalog, I guess they are also used in electronics.<P>Where on your fiero did you find these screws?<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||151 in. of love||02-13-2001||02:39 PM||||Yup.<P>We have those to keep the winows shut here in the clink. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(safety torx) found everywhere<BR>I don't think I have ever noticed them on anything but a DODGE.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||02-13-2001||03:39 PM||||If you look at the screws that hold the cable to your deck lid you'll see the torx safety screws.||||reg||6
Z||000009||stsmithgt||02-13-2001||03:43 PM||||Those security torx bolts are used a lot in housings for electronic equipment to prevent tampering.  The torx security bits have been available at a store called Orchard Supply Hardware.  Sears bought them out awhile back so I don't know if they still carry them or even it that store is in your area.  Maybe  Sears has them now.  One of the techs I work with  brought it to my attention that those security torx work great in small sizes, but the larger ones you can fit(jam) a screw driver into them to unscrew them.||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierospeeder||02-13-2001||04:23 PM||||go to <A HREF="http://www.jcwhitney.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jcwhitney.com</A> <P>and on the left side, you can type in item numbers and go to the description and be able to purchase it online<P><BR>try these part #s<P>12bs9643U 24.99  10 pc<BR>88bs8947r 11.99  15 pc<BR>14bs8543n 15.99  08 pc <BR>81bs3896p 03.99  07 pc||||reg||1
Z||000011||Philphine||02-13-2001||04:51 PM||||got 'em. auto zone. thanks everyone.||||reg||1
